WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.174
Hey Youtubers! This is Charlie.

00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:07.600
So hopefully you have all had a chance to see episode 1 of Korra Book 4.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.100
This is gonna be my review.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.200
And just because this is the first episode and there is a lot of stuff to get through I made it a little bit longer.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.623
And there is gonna be a top 10.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.107
Heads up too. It looks like Amazon is gonna be releasing episodes at midnight pacific time.

00:00:20.107 --> 00:00:23.133
That's Thursday night or Friday morning. However you look at it.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.400
Nickelodeon posts them on their website a little before noon.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.000
So, if you are willing to pay a couple of dollars extra, you can watch the episode 

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.100
like 8-12 hours before everyone else.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.500
And again I know you guys all be happy to know the weekly giveaway is back.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.640
All you have to do is enter, is be a subscriber and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.000
I'll announce the winner whenever I post my Q&amp;A tomorrow.

00:00:40.174 --> 00:00:42.973
But... Careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the episode yet.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:44.820
Okay. Here we go.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.293
Top 10 moments: Number 10.

00:00:46.293 --> 00:00:47.254
Three years later.

00:00:47.254 --> 00:00:49.275
The high speed rail system,

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.500
Team Korra being pulled in all different directions,

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.300
the new Earth Kingdom prince,

00:00:54.453 --> 00:00:57.874
And Kuvira's mission to fix the mess in the Earth Kingdom.

00:00:57.874 --> 00:01:01.153
The world has changed a lot and the characters have changed a lot.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.040
Number 9: Meet Wu prince of the Earth Kingdom.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.500
I couldn't find any information on who the voice actor was

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.654
but I'll try to find out by the time I post my Q&amp;A video Saturday.

00:01:09.654 --> 00:01:11.994
Or if you do know just write it in the comments.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.900
There is a whole lot to say about him.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.994
But he gives all kind of exposition about what's been happening in the Earth Kingdom.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.160
Kuvira has been cleaning up the mess

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.660
and he has been living in exile.

00:01:21.248 --> 00:01:23.388
We also find out how he is related to Hou-Ting.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.606
They are like distant relatives, distant cousins.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.320
So he probably just came from one of really wealthy families in Ba Sing Se.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.100
Based on the rest of the episode 

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.900
it seems like he is going to be on one side of the conflict and Kuvira on the other.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.740
With the prise being the throne of the Earth Kingdom.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.000
The whole scene with the pies just let us know

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.400
that Kuvira has pretty much won over the populace.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.500
Like she is gonna get the popular vote.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.760
But president Reiko from Republic City is backing Wu.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.100
So, I am wondering if the other nations of the world are gonna back him too. 

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:57.380
It's probably just because he feels like Wu is much easier to deal with than a really powerful war lord.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.280
I don't think that president Reiko is gonna be a villian or anything,

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.660
I just think he is a politician through and through.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.240
If you remenber that trailer scene with Zuko, his daughter and president Reiko.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.900
It seems like other nations are gonna back Wu.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.340
And that's gonna cause the greater conflict. That's gonna be like the spark in the flame.

00:02:12.393 --> 00:02:14.073
It's gonna set Book 4 off.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:19.340
It'll be like the politicians of the world versus Kuvira and her army of the people.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.720
Number 8: Team Korra montage.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.940
So we start learning where everyone is and how they've changed.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.740
Three years does not sound like a lot but

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.540
everyone is little bit more mature

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.140
and they have gone from teenagers arguing about relationships

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.520
to young adults arguing about politics.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.100
I also saw that a bunch of you were confused about some scenes in the trailers

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.120
where looked like Team Korra people were fighting each other.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.414
That's not the case and I'll totally explain it.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.500
You can see though how that might end up happening

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.741
based on everyone getting pulled in different directions.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:51.260
Team Korra is not gonna be broken apart for that long.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.954
Like they'll get back together eventually.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.120
Number 7: Kai and Opal to the rescue.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:00.020
So this was just like Mako's intro scene during Book 2 all over again.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.220
He gets that really cool motorcycle chase intro

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.110
when he does that

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.733
big, you know firebending take down of those criminals.

00:03:06.733 --> 00:03:08.534
The Triple Threat Triads I think.

00:03:09.036 --> 00:03:11.036
Kai and Opal exact same thing.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.026
I really am stoked about these new airbender costumes.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:17.200
They're gonna stand out really nicely against the metalbending army.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.850
But there are just so many awsome things to talk about.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:23.100
About just where the Air Nation is right now and it's state of developement.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.940
They're basically like super cops, now being dispached all over the Earth Kingdom by Tenzin.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.600
And you can tell they are pros too. Like they have been doing this for a long time. They're really good.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.214
Even though they've did loose those supplies.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.620
I think that was just to show that they were fighting a battle that they couldn't win.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:40.758
Like you were supposed to feel like the mayor had no other choice but to sign Kuvira's deal.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.660
Number 6: Tenzin's family all have grown up.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.214
I love seeing Rohan with hair, like we haven't seen him in a long time.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:52.340
And then there is Milo, who looks like he's about the same age as Kai was during Book 3.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:57.896
Milo the boy becoming Milo the man was probably the best animation sequence in the episode.

00:03:57.896 --> 00:03:59.853
At least next to Kuvira's fight.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.920
We also get a really good look at Jinora with her hair again too.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.740
I know some people really didn't like her being bald.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:09.267
I didn't have too many issues with it. But she did look exactly like Aang.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:12.067
But I think that was the point. I think she was supposed to look like Aang.

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:14.034
Or she was supposed to remind us of Aang.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.460
Number 5: Mako is getting sent to Ba Sing Se on permanent duty.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.698
Just one more nail in the coffin of Team Korra.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.400
This is gonna put Mako and Bolin in direct opposition to each other.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.374
Brother against brother.

00:04:26.374 --> 00:04:29.494
It's just like Opal's brother is on the opposite side from her.

00:04:29.494 --> 00:04:32.434
Like families are going to be in conflict this season.

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:35.114
It's a lot like the United States civil war.

00:04:35.114 --> 00:04:38.193
You know. Politics dividing families, dividing the country.

00:04:38.193 --> 00:04:42.100
Like is said earlier though, I don't think Team Korra is gonna beat each other throats for too long.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.976
I do think they're gonna have a happy ending.

00:04:43.976 --> 00:04:46.430
But, things are gonna get worse before they'll get better.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.660
Number 4: Meet Team Kuvira.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.014
Think about Team Kuvira as being an analog of Team Korra.

00:04:53.014 --> 00:04:54.998
Or even Team Zaheer for that matter.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:59.140
But it's Bolin, Varrick, Zhu Li and one of Opal's brothers.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.900
Not Skrillex, I think his name is Bataar.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:07.120
The perspective shifts a couple of times. But we're mostly seeing her inner circle from Bolin's perspective.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:11.500
I am already starting to get a little bit nervous about what's gonna happen to Team Korra though.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.460
The train itself looked amazing, like the high-speed rail.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:20.673
I got the sense that visually the train was also supposed to represent the unstoppable nature of Kuvira this season.

00:05:20.673 --> 00:05:23.652
Like even rocks on the tracks weren't enough to stop her.

00:05:23.652 --> 00:05:26.474
She is just metalbending the shit out of everything in her path.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.940
Speking of which. Number 3: Kuvira versus the bandits.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.940
Probably one of the coolest uses of metalbending that I have ever seen.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:38.400
It reminded me of Book 1 when we saw Korra using more sophisticated bending techniques,

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.919
than we have seen on Last Airbender.

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:43.639
And like the metalbending police force, going all Spider-man with their cables.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:48.780
It just becomes pretty clear that Kuvira is doing everything she can to bring the Earth Kingdom to heel.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:52.500
Those bandits were so quick to accept her offer of joining the army.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.200
It's sounds like just everyone in general in the Earth Kingdom want some relief.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.516
Like they want some directions, someone to lead them.

00:05:58.516 --> 00:06:00.438
And they really don't care who helps them out.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.153
The result is that Kuvira is just constantly adding to her forces.

00:06:04.153 --> 00:06:07.875
Whether it be the bandints or the states themselves and all the supplies.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.560
It wasn't really clear when she had that conversation with the mayor, but

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:15.155
the contract said that they had to give her supplies and manpower.

00:06:15.155 --> 00:06:16.935
Like that what she was taking from them.

00:06:17.354 --> 00:06:20.554
Number 2: Kuvira's unification plan revealed.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:24.800
So she making all the states swear allegiance in exchange for protection.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.969
It's technically not blackmail.

00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:29.179
Unless she sends bandits back to the city.

00:06:29.179 --> 00:06:31.705
And that doesn't seem like her flavour of evil.

00:06:31.705 --> 00:06:33.695
It feels like something Varrick would have done.

00:06:33.994 --> 00:06:38.474
Like whenever he had people hijack Asami's shipments back in Book 2, so she'd go bankrupt.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:41.100
Remember he also framed Mako for that.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.520
Based on that lego map that Kuvira was putting together...

00:06:44.524 --> 00:06:46.753
And yes, it did look like she was playing with legos.

00:06:46.753 --> 00:06:48.633
She is almost done with her mission.

00:06:48.633 --> 00:06:51.274
Like she's almost completely unified the Earth Kingdom.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.280
The tease being that if she completes the job...

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.617
She'll have all the combined resources of the Earth Kingdom at her disposal,

00:06:58.617 --> 00:07:00.033
including their manpower.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.702
Most notably their manpower.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:08.000
So the potential is that she'll decide that she is a better candidate to lead the Earth Kingdom than Wu is.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.560
And you get your conflict.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:15.280
Like she can raise up an army to fight off any invading force, trying to install Wu on the throne.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.620
Which in this case might end up being the Republic City forces.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.835
Who just happened to be commanded by Zuko's grandson.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.780
We'll have to see how that plays out.

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:26.080
They didn't come right out and say: Kuvira is not gonna give up 

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.070
controll over the Earth Kingdom when she is done.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.921
But she is the villain. So it's gonna happen pretty soon.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.360
And my number 1 moment - of course: Korra is an underground MMA bender.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.340
Kuvira's been getting sharper - literally.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.867
And Korra looks like she is barely treading water.

00:07:40.867 --> 00:07:41.720
Not good.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.000
I totally love the WTF reveal though, of what she's been doing the last six months.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.340
Just basically getting the crap beat out of her.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.980
In the trailer we a saw a big spirit world montage.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:56.272
If anyone saw Superman 2, like the really old Superman movie with Christopher Reeve.

00:07:56.272 --> 00:07:59.194
He basically gave up his powers to become human,

00:07:59.194 --> 00:08:01.734
but found out that the world still needed him to be Superman.

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:05.917
So he literally had to hitchhike all the way back to the fortress of solitude

00:08:05.917 --> 00:08:07.335
to get his powers back.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.580
Just like we see Korra here marching through the snow back to the spirit portal.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.820
So, yes she is definitely gonna get her mojo back at some point,

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.699
but she gonna have to have a call to action.

00:08:17.004 --> 00:08:20.604
Something has to change to slap her in the face and wake her up because

00:08:20.604 --> 00:08:22.834
right now it looks like she is completely lost.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.000
Let me know what your favorite moment was.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.200
There is a whole lot to pick from.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:29.117
And let me know, what do you think is gonna be the big call to action, 

00:08:29.117 --> 00:08:31.261
that's gonna make Korra go back to the spirit portal.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.860
Overall I gave the episode a solid A.

00:08:33.869 --> 00:08:36.160
I totally love the way, they got through all that exposition.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.509
And reintroduced us to the characters and the state of the world.

00:08:39.509 --> 00:08:42.360
It's like they are just setting up a giant pai sho board.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.354
And now we get to watch the game unfold.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.500
Infact, if you actually rewatch the episode of Book 3

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.434
when Asami and Bolin play pai sho.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.840
She has this really good speech about what it takes to win a game.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:56.233
I bet there is a really good lesson in there for what's gonna happen in Book 4.

00:08:57.271 --> 00:09:01.431
So here's a clarification from some of those scenes in the trailer that everyone was confused about.

00:09:01.431 --> 00:09:02.991
Cause we actually got most of it answered.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.619
So first off, here is Korra in her MMA outfit in the swamps.

00:09:07.619 --> 00:09:09.454
Looking like she gonna get her butt kicked.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:12.040
Especially when she gets captured in liquid metal.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.360
Here we see Bolin jumping to escape from one of the giant mechs.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.280
You can kinda see him jump down. It's a little fuzzy.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.900
Maybe he turns against Kuvira soon.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:23.737
Clearly someone else from the army is after him.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.620
This person on the train that Asami is fighting with the short hair, that's Opal's brother.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:32.280
I konw everyone wondered if it was Bolin or Mako.

00:09:32.391 --> 00:09:33.831
Thankfully it is not.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.700
This here though with Korra is Mako at this White Lotus Temple.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.000
No idea where it is located though.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:45.420
This Toph scene also kinda looks like it came after that big swamp fight scene.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.904
Just because she looks like she got the crap beat out of her.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:52.320
So yes. I mean Team Avatar is gonna be pushed apart by all these political forces.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.000
But they will come back together eventually.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.200
I'm hoping it's like maybe the third or fourth episode when we see that.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:57.854
But who knows.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.960
So really good news, for any fans of the comic book.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:05.660
Bryan Konietzko basically said that he is gonna double down on the comic book.

00:10:05.665 --> 00:10:07.420
After Korra Book 4 is out.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.160
Like he is hoping to work more on the comic book.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.520
So I know a lot of people were wondering what's gonna happen with the comics.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:15.860
They will continue.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:20.020
If you are wondering where to buy them. You can just get them on Comixology online.

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:22.195
If your local comic book shop doesn't have them.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.780
I will be posting a Q&amp;A for this tomorrow. So be sure to leave all your questions.

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:28.613
There is a whole lot of stuff to talk about.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.960
Right now click here to get to that video. I'll add the annotation as soon as I post it.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:36.222
And you can click here for my top 10 avatar villains.

00:10:36.222 --> 00:10:37.502
Thank you so much for watching.

00:10:37.502 --> 00:10:38.667
So let's all high five.

00:10:38.667 --> 00:10:40.959
Do not forget: Star Wars Rebels tonight.

00:10:41.007 --> 00:10:42.000
Be sure to watch it.

